<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <!--
      Entitlements for the bare `anglesite-remote-helper` SwiftPM executable when it is spawned
      as a second process by HelperContainerE2ETests (#1208 P1 exit criterion).

      Same rationale as Resources/container-probe.entitlements: swiftpm-testing-helper (the
      process `swift test` actually runs) cannot carry com.apple.security.virtualization, so a
      test that boots a container has to put the entitlement on a *separate* binary it spawns.
      Here that binary is the helper itself, which calls ContainerizationControl.start() — an
      unsigned `swift build` product would fail with LocalContainerError.virtualizationUnavailable
      before ever reaching a VM. The test ad-hoc code-signs the built binary against this file
      (an ad-hoc `codesign` invocation passing this path as its entitlements) exactly as
      scripts/run-container-probe.sh does for anglesite-container-probe. Note the comment text
      here must avoid a doubled hyphen: AMFI's XML parser rejects one inside a comment, which is
      illegal XML, and codesign then fails with "AMFIUnserializeXML: syntax error".

      Deliberately NOT Resources/AnglesiteRemote.entitlements: that one is for the real, bundled,
      provisioned `Anglesite Remote.app` and declares com.apple.security.app-sandbox. Sandboxing
      a bare, non-bundled CLI with no provisioning profile is a different (and broken) code path,
      so — like container-probe.entitlements — this file stays minimal and sandbox-free.

      Networking is included on top of the probe's single entitlement because the helper does more
      than boot a VM: it dials the container's loopback preview/MCP ports (client) and terminates
      a real WebRTC peer connection (server).
    -->

    <key>com.apple.security.virtualization</key><true/>
    <key>com.apple.security.network.client</key><true/>
    <key>com.apple.security.network.server</key><true/>
</dict>
</plist>
